<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24769" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-vincĭbĭlis</span></b> ,
		e, adj.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Invincible</i>, <i>unconquerable</i>
			(post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">invincibile et insuperabile malum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Herm. 11</span></i>
			. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Irrefutable</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gravia et invincibilia dicere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Mag. p. 297</span></i>
			.—<i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">invin-cĭbĭlĭter</span></b> , <i>irrefutably</i>, <i><span class="en">App. Flor.
				p. 360, 31</span></i>. </div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
